# Folder & Naming Structure (Permanent)

## `apps/api` (NestJS)

```text
apps/api/
  src/
    main.ts
    app.module.ts
    common/                 # guards, filters, pipes, decorators, interceptors
    config/                 # edition, db, redis, mongo config
    modules/
      identity/
      tenancy/
      billing/
      content/
      assets/
      design/
      documents/
      export/
      audit/
      system/
    prisma/                 # if Prisma — schema + migrations (or ../prisma)
  test/
```

Inside each `modules/{context}/`:

```text
{context}.module.ts
{context}.controller.ts     # thin
{context}.service.ts
dto/
entities/ or repositories/
guards/                     # only if module-specific
```

- Controllers stay thin: validate DTO → service → response.
- Prefer use-case services over god services.
- PostgreSQL migrations via Prisma Migrate (or TypeORM migrations) — always include `businessId` where tenant-owned.
- Mongo schemas/collections live under `documents` (and related) modules.

## `apps/web` (Next.js App Router)

```text
apps/web/
  src/
    app/                    # App Router: [locale]/ layouts, pages
      [locale]/
        (auth)/
        (app)/              # authenticated shell
    features/
      auth/
      businesses/
      billing/
      content/
      editor/
      media/
      settings/
    shared/
      api/                  # fetch/client, React Query if used
      ui/                   # design-system (theme tokens)
      i18n/                 # next-intl messages fa/en
      lib/
      types/
    styles/                 # global tokens light/dark
```

- Feature folders own UI + hooks for that feature.
- No deep imports across features; share only via `shared/` or `packages/*`.
- Editor under `features/editor/`.
- Theme + i18n providers in root/`[locale]` layout — see `10-theme-and-i18n.mdc`.

## Docs (repo root)

```text
docs/
  api/                 # OpenAPI — MUST stay current
  deploy/
  adr/
```

## Naming

- TS everywhere: `PascalCase` classes/components; `camelCase` methods/fields in code; DB columns `snake_case` in PostgreSQL via Prisma `@map` if needed; Mongo field `businessId` camelCase consistent in app layer.
- `businessId` everywhere tenant-scoped (API + PG + Mongo).
- Routes: `/api/...` Nest global prefix; business-scoped resources under `/businesses/:businessId/...`.
- Entitlement codes: `module.map`, `module.org_chart`, `export.pdf`.

## Forbidden layouts

- Do not create a Vite-SPA parallel app as the primary web.
- Do not put Nest domain logic inside Next Route Handlers except BFF-thin proxies if explicitly needed — default: browser → Nest API.
- Do not dump all code in one `controllers/` flat folder without modules.
